Conclusion: for a non-declaration transpile, the diagnostics that syntaxErrors reads are computed before the emit and do not depend on any transformer; the JS emit contributes none, so the EMPTY_EMIT 'before' transformer cannot hide a diagnostic. A residual: the old path also exercised the printer, so a TypeScript emitter crash on syntactically valid source would have thrown in the old path and no longer does; that is not a syntax diagnostic and rule 4 never reported it as one.
